      ":question/worked-solution": "Let's analyze each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false. The root $x=-5$ is a simple root because the graph crosses the $x$-axis at the point and the curve is not tangent to the $x$-axis at that point. The root $x=2$ has an odd multiplicity because the graph passes through the $x$-axis at this point. The curve is tangent to the $x$-axis at that point, so the root is not simple.\n\n- Statement II is true. The root $x=-4$ has an even multiplicity because at $x=-4$ the graph just touches the $x$-axis and reverses direction.\n\n- Statement III is true. As $x$ moves left in the negative direction towards $-\\infty,$ the $y$ value moves down in the negative direction towards $-\\infty.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only\".",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
        {
          ":answer-field/id": "1d5ac3f8-8bbe-5369-b41f-776b285d9c9e",
          ":answer-field/key": "I",
